---
// AWS User Group Mysuru follows the AWS Code of Conduct. The policy text below
// is reproduced verbatim from https://aws.amazon.com/codeofconduct/ — update it
// from the source (and the "Last Updated" date) if AWS revises it.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';

const SOURCE = 'https://aws.amazon.com/codeofconduct/';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Code of Conduct"
  description="AWS User Group Mysuru follows the AWS Code of Conduct at all of its meetups, workshops and online spaces."
>
  <header class="page-hero container">
    <span class="eyebrow">Community</span>
    <h1>Code of Conduct</h1>
    <p>
      {SITE.name} follows the{' '}
      <a href={SOURCE} rel="noopener">
        AWS Code of Conduct
      </a>{' '}
      at all of our meetups, workshops and online spaces.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="container">
    <article class="prose coc" aria-labelledby="coc-title">
      <h2 id="coc-title">AWS Code of Conduct</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        <strong>Last Updated: June 4, 2026</strong>
      </p>

      <h3>Importance</h3>
      <p>
        We firmly believe in the value and importance of an environment where all AWS community
        members feel welcome and safe. This Code of Conduct explains the behavior we expect from AWS
        community members interacting at AWS events and programs, and across AWS blogs, online
        forums, and social media platforms (collectively, AWS Programs). The purpose of AWS Programs
        is to foster technical and professional education and encourage community discussion.
      </p>

      <h3>Behavior</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>
          You will behave in a way that facilitates a safe and supportive environment for all AWS
          Program participants.
        </li>
        <li>
          You will not engage in disruptive speech or behavior or otherwise interfere with other
          individuals' participation in AWS Program.
        </li>
        <li>You will not interfere with the operation of AWS Programs.</li>
        <li>
          You will provide accurate and truthful information during registration, check-in, or login
          for any AWS Program.
        </li>
        <li>
          You will only use the AWS Program credentials (e.g., event badges, login information to
          programs or communities) that are provided to you. You will not transfer, lend, or share
          your AWS Program credentials with anyone.
        </li>
        <li>
          You will not attempt to receive benefits that you are not entitled to in relation to any
          AWS Program.
        </li>
        <li>
          You will not engage in any form of harassing, offensive, discriminatory, or threatening
          speech or behavior, including but not limited to relating to race, gender, gender identity
          and expression, national origin, religion, disability, marital status, age, sexual
          orientation, military or veteran status, or other protected category.
        </li>
        <li>
          Unless you are a registered AWS Event Sponsor, you will not use any AWS Program to market,
          promote, advertise, solicit, or distribute materials regarding your own products,
          services, or offerings, or those of any third party, without AWS's prior written consent.
        </li>
        <li>
          You will comply with the instructions of AWS Program staff, including event and program
          staff and AWS blog, online forum, and social media platform moderators.
        </li>
        <li>
          You will comply with all applicable laws and any AWS Program specific requirements
          (including all health and safety requirements).
        </li>
      </ol>

      <h3>Scope</h3>
      <p>
        We expect all AWS community members (including but not limited to attendees, vendors,
        sponsors, speakers, volunteers, moderators, and AWS employees) to uphold the principles of
        this Code of Conduct. This Code of Conduct covers the main AWS Program and all related AWS
        Programs (e.g., main events along with all related events or activities, social or
        otherwise). AWS employees must continue to abide by all company policies at all times.
      </p>

      <h3>Consequences</h3>
      <p>If we believe you breached this Code of Conduct, we may do any of the following:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Require you to leave or stop participating in an AWS Program that you are currently
          participating in;
        </li>
        <li>Prohibit you from attending or participating in future AWS Programs; or</li>
        <li>
          Remove any content you submitted, posted, or otherwise made available within an AWS
          Program in violation of this Code of Conduct.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If we require you to leave an AWS event, you will not be eligible to receive a refund of any
        fees paid to us related to the event. All determinations are at our sole discretion. We will
        involve law enforcement if we deem appropriate.
      </p>

      <h3>Contact Us</h3>
      <p>
        If you witness or are subjected to inappropriate behavior at any AWS Program, please
        promptly contact AWS at{' '}
        <a href="mailto:aws-events-security-concerns@amazon.com">
          aws-events-security-concerns@amazon.com
        </a>
        .
      </p>
    </article>

    <aside class="coc-note">
      <p>
        At {SITE.name} events you can also speak to any organiser, or email{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Source:{' '}
        <a href={SOURCE} rel="noopener">
          aws.amazon.com/codeofconduct
        </a>
      </p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .coc {
    max-width: 46rem;
  }

  .coc h3 {
    margin-top: 1.8em;
  }

  .coc ol li {
    padding-left: 0.25em;
  }

  .coc-note {
    max-width: 46rem;
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-5);
    border: 1px solid var(--c-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--c-bg-alt);
    color: var(--c-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }
</style>
